// The hiring framework's own surface (FSD §5.15;
// docs/framework-research/14-schema-rendering.md §3).
//
// The JD reviewer structures a posting into requirements and judges a
// candidate's evidence against each one. This service is where a person
// on the hiring side works on those requirements as rows: reads what
// the extraction drafted, corrects it, and releases it for judging.
// Every edit is a new version, a judgment names the version it judged,
// and the extractor's draft and the person's edit are both kept, so the
// reason for an edit feeds extractor calibration instead of vanishing
// (J8).
//
// It is a service of its own rather than more methods on JdService
// because the member's submit-and-poll flow and the hiring side's
// editing flow have different callers and different rules (14 §3.3).
// Phase 0 step 5 lands the requirement methods and the settings; the
// match record, overrides, the clarification loop and the catalog
// follow in steps 6 to 8.
//
// Vocabulary codes (type, class, threshold units) travel as strings,
// not enums: the vocabulary is data in `vocab_codes`, a new code must
// not be a proto change, and a reader keeps a code it does not know
// (14 §3.1). The codes of vocabulary 1.1 are listed in the field
// comments; the registry is the source of record.

